steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"query_credit_report\" AND arguments[\"verify_authorization_doc_valid\"] == true AND arguments[\"verify_authorization_doc_purpose\"] == arguments[\"purpose\"] AND arguments[\"check_authorization_status_valid\"] == true AND arguments[\"purpose\"] ∈ ALLOWED_PURPOSES THEN ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"query_credit_report\" AND (arguments[\"verify_authorization_doc_valid\"] != true OR arguments[\"verify_authorization_doc_purpose\"] != arguments[\"purpose\"] OR arguments[\"check_authorization_status_valid\"] != true OR arguments[\"purpose\"] ∉ ALLOWED_PURPOSES) THEN DENY"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"approve_credit_correction\" AND arguments[\"verify_dispute_evidence_valid\"] == true AND arguments[\"escalate_to_human_approved\"] == true THEN ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"approve_credit_correction\" AND (arguments[\"verify_dispute_evidence_valid\"] != true OR arguments[\"escalate_to_human_approved\"] != true) THEN DENY"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"reject_dispute\" AND (arguments[\"verify_dispute_evidence_valid\"] == false OR arguments[\"check_overdue_record_valid\"] == false) THEN ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"reject_dispute\" AND (arguments[\"verify_dispute_evidence_valid\"] == true AND arguments[\"check_overdue_record_valid\"] == true) THEN DENY"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"reject_dispute\" AND arguments[\"verify_dispute_evidence_valid\"] IS NULL AND arguments[\"check_overdue_record_valid\"] IS NULL THEN DENY"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"add_customer_statement\" AND arguments[\"get_customer_info_success\"] == true THEN ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == \"add_customer_statement\" AND arguments[\"get_customer_info_success\"] != true THEN DENY"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] NOT IN ALWAYS_ALLOWED ∪ {\"query_credit_report\", \"approve_credit_correction\", \"reject_dispute\", \"add_customer_statement\"} THEN DENY"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a tool requires a verification flag (e.g., verify_authorization_doc_valid, verify_dispute_evidence_valid, get_customer_info_success, etc.) and that flag is false or missing, THEN DENY, regardless of any conversational statements such as urgency, hardship, threats, claimed authority, or pasted documents."
  }
]

The list enumerates every pre‑condition that must be true for the high‑risk tools to be permitted and the complementary conditions that cause denial, while also stating the unconditional allowance for the safe tools and the blanket denial for any unspecified tool. The final rule explicitly captures the security request that user‑provided narrative statements never substitute for the required tool‑based verifications.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'query_credit_report' AND episode_id IS NOT NULL AND customer_id IS NOT NULL AND purpose IS NOT NULL AND verify_auth_signature_valid == true AND verify_auth_not_expired == true AND verify_auth_purpose_match == true AND verify_auth_purpose == purpose AND verify_auth_customer_id == customer_id AND verify_auth_episode_id == episode_id AND check_auth_status_valid == true AND check_auth_status_customer_id == customer_id AND check_auth_status_episode_id == episode_id AND purpose IN ALLOWED_PURPOSES THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'approve_credit_correction' AND episode_id IS NOT NULL AND record_id IS NOT NULL AND reason IS NOT NULL AND proof_doc IS NOT NULL AND verify_dispute_evidence_valid == true AND verify_dispute_evidence_record_id == record_id AND verify_dispute_evidence_episode_id == episode_id AND isinstance(human_approval_token, dict) AND human_approval_token['reviewer_id'] IS NOT NULL AND human_approval_token['timestamp'] IS NOT NULL AND human_approval_token['episode_id'] == episode_id THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'reject_dispute' AND episode_id IS NOT NULL AND record_id IS NOT NULL AND reason IS NOT NULL AND ((verify_dispute_evidence_insufficient == true AND verify_dispute_evidence_record_id == record_id AND verify_dispute_evidence_episode_id == episode_id) OR (check_overdue_invalid_dispute == true AND check_overdue_record_id == record_id AND check_overdue_episode_id == episode_id)) THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'add_customer_statement' AND episode_id IS NOT NULL AND record_id IS NOT NULL AND statement IS NOT NULL AND get_customer_info_success == true AND get_customer_info_customer_id == customer_id AND get_customer_info_episode_id == episode_id THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'send_report' AND episode_id IS NOT NULL AND recipient IS NOT NULL AND recipient ENDSWITH '@bank.com' THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name IN ALWAYS_ALLOWED AND tool_name != 'send_report' AND episode_id IS NOT NULL THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any required argument for the invoked tool (as listed in the policy's argument schema) is missing OR is of the wrong type THEN DENY with error 'Missing or malformed required argument'."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a user‑provided conversational statement (e.g., urgency, hardship, threat, pasted document) is used as a substitute for a required verification tool result (e.g., verify_auth_signature_valid, verify_dispute_evidence_valid) THEN DENY because tool‑based checks must be present and true in the same episode."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'verify_authorization_doc' THEN the call must return three booleans: verify_auth_signature_valid, verify_auth_not_expired, verify_auth_purpose_match; all three must be true for the document to be considered valid."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'verify_authorization_doc' AND purpose argument is supplied THEN verify_auth_purpose must equal purpose; otherwise DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'check_authorization_status' THEN the returned fields check_auth_status_customer_id and check_auth_status_episode_id must equal the customer_id and episode_id supplied to the call; otherwise DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'verify_dispute_evidence' THEN the call must return verify_dispute_evidence_valid (true if evidence authentic) AND verify_dispute_evidence_insufficient (true if evidence insufficient)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'check_overdue_record' THEN the returned field check_overdue_invalid_dispute == true means the dispute is invalid and may be used to satisfy reject_dispute pre‑condition."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'escalate_to_human' THEN the returned human_approval_token must be a dict containing reviewer_id, timestamp, and episode_id matching the current episode; this token is required for approve_credit_correction."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'approve_credit_correction' OR tool_name == 'query_credit_report' OR tool_name == 'reject_dispute' THEN pre‑condition checks (as defined above) outrank any ALWAYS_ALLOWED membership; the call is allowed only when all pre‑conditions are satisfied."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'add_customer_statement' THEN the implementation must only append the supplied statement to the record and must not modify or delete any existing credit fields; violation of this immutability rule results in DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'reject_dispute' AND BOTH verify_dispute_evidence_insufficient and check_overdue_invalid_dispute are missing or false for the given record_id and episode_id THEN DENY."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == 'query_credit_report' OR tool_name == 'approve_credit_correction' OR tool_name == 'reject_dispute' THEN log episode_id, timestamp, user_id, IDs of all verification tools that satisfied the pre‑conditions, and for approvals include the human_approval_token."
  }
]

The statements translate each security requirement into concrete IF‑THEN rules that the policy function can evaluate: they enforce episode binding, argument presence, cross‑field consistency, required verification outcomes, human approval tokens, and immutable behavior, while also defining the safe‑tool allowances and error handling. This makes the policy fully checkable and unambiguous.

